9️⃣ Common Interview Questions
What is DLQ?

A mechanism to store failed messages after retries.

Why is DLQ important?

Prevents data loss and isolates failures.

Difference: Retry vs DLQ
Feature	Retry	DLQ
Purpose	Try again	Store failed messages
When used	Temporary failures	Permanent failures
How many retries?

Depends on system (usually 3–5).

