2️⃣ ISR (In-Sync Replicas)
What is ISR?

Each Kafka partition has:

Leader → Handles reads/writes
Followers → Replicate data

👉 ISR = replicas that are fully synced with leader

Example
Partition-0:
Leader → Broker-1
Followers → Broker-2, Broker-3

ISR = [1,2,3]
Important Config
min.insync.replicas=2

👉 Meaning:

At least 2 replicas must acknowledge

Otherwise → write FAIL ❌

Why Important?
Leader crashes → Another ISR becomes leader → No data loss
3️⃣ acks (Acknowledgment Levels)

This controls when producer considers message successful

🔹 acks = 0
Producer → Fire and forget
No confirmation

❌ Risk: Data loss

🔹 acks = 1
Leader writes → ACK sent
Followers may not have data

⚠️ Risk: If leader crashes → data loss

🔹 acks = all (Recommended ✅)
Leader + ISR replicas confirm

✔ No data loss (if ISR maintained)

Production Rule
acks=all
4️⃣ Retries

If sending fails:

retries=5
retry.backoff.ms=1000

👉 Meaning:

Retry 5 times

Wait 1 sec between retries

Important

Without retries:

Temporary network issue → message lost ❌
5️⃣ Idempotent Producer (VERY IMPORTANT)
Problem

Retries can cause duplicates:

Send → Timeout → Retry → Same message sent again
Solution
enable.idempotence=true

👉 Kafka ensures:

✔ No duplicate messages
✔ Exactly-once per partition

Behind the scenes

Kafka uses:

Producer ID

Sequence numbers

6️⃣ Complete Production Producer Config
spring:
  kafka:
    producer:
      bootstrap-servers: localhost:9092
      key-serializer: org.apache.kafka.common.serialization.StringSerializer
      value-serializer: org.springframework.kafka.support.serializer.JsonSerializer

      acks: all
      retries: 5
      properties:
        enable.idempotence: true
        max.in.flight.requests.per.connection: 5
        retry.backoff.ms: 1000
        delivery.timeout.ms: 120000
        linger.ms: 5
        batch.size: 16384
7️⃣ Consumer Production Config
spring:
  kafka:
    consumer:
      bootstrap-servers: localhost:9092
      group-id: transaction-group
      auto-offset-reset: earliest
      enable-auto-commit: false

      properties:
        max.poll.records: 100
Manual Commit (BEST PRACTICE)
@KafkaListener(topics = "transaction-events")
public void consume(ConsumerRecord<String, String> record,
                    Acknowledgment ack) {

    try {
        process(record.value());
        ack.acknowledge(); // commit offset manually
    } catch (Exception e) {
        throw e; // goes to retry/DLQ
    }
}
8️⃣ Exactly-Once vs At-Least-Once
Mode	Config	Guarantee
At-most-once	auto commit	No duplicates, possible loss
At-least-once	retries + manual commit	No loss, duplicates possible
Exactly-once	idempotence + transactions	No loss, no duplicates
