1️⃣1️⃣ Common Mistakes (VERY IMPORTANT)

❌ acks=1 → Data loss risk
❌ retries=0 → No fault tolerance
❌ idempotence=false → Duplicate transactions
❌ auto-commit=true → Message loss

1️⃣2️⃣ Interview Answer (🔥 GOLD)

👉 “How do you configure Kafka for production?”

We use acks=all with min.insync.replicas to ensure durability,
enable idempotence to avoid duplicates,
configure retries with backoff for transient failures,
and use manual offset commit with DLQ handling for consumers.
